  "Which license does sqll use? The repository has no license file. It must permit the Apache-2.0 duties (option 1) or the MIT duties (options 2 and 3), and those of the dependencies.",
  "Option 1: the sqruff crates port sqlfluff code and ship sqlfluff fixture files with no sqlfluff MIT notice. Must sqll add the sqlfluff MIT notice for the parts that it takes from sqruff? sqll already carries it for its own ports (THIRD_PARTY.md).",
  "Options 2 and 3: are the generated dialect tables a substantial portion of sqlfluff, so that each sqll binary must carry the sqlfluff MIT notice?",
  "How does a sqll binary give the notices of its dependencies (MIT, BSD, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, Apache-2.0)? For example a notices file made at release time.",
  "The sqlfluffrs crates have no license field in Cargo.toml. Does sqlfluffrs/LICENSE.md (MIT, named by sqlfluffrs/pyproject.toml) cover each Rust crate of the workspace?",
  "For each dependency with an OR choice that has a copyleft option (permissive_choice_over), sqll takes the permissive option. Must the choice be recorded?",
